<li>Thread within the same process share a common address space, data segment and heap.&nbsp;Inter-thread communication occurs via shared memory without IPC mechanisms. Threads&nbsp;can directly access global variable and shared data structures. Communication overhead is&nbsp;lower compared to inter-process communication. So, option (d) is correct.</li>
