            solution: `<p>All processes enter the ready queue at time 0, so initially their waiting times and priorities are&nbsp;equal. Since the scheduler is non-preemptive, the first selected process runs to completion, and&nbsp;the others in the ready queue accumulative waiting time, the execution order therefore follows&nbsp;arrival order, making it equivalent to FCFS. Because priority increases with waiting time, every&nbsp;process eventually get CPU time, so no starvation occurs.</p>`
